 "char": {
  "id": "dot",
  "handle": "dot_on_the_dial",
  "name": "Dot",
  "bio": "Forty years of listening to the sky.",
  "voice": "af_sarah",
  "case": "wow",
  "look": {
   "skin": "#e8c4a8",
   "hair": "#d9d6cf",
   "style": "bob",
   "shirt": "#3b5b7a",
   "glasses": true,
   "extra": "headphones"
  },
  "script": "I spent forty years listening to the sky on a radio, and I still think about one night. August fifteenth, 1977. The Big Ear telescope in Ohio picked up a signal so strong and so narrow that the astronomer circled it and wrote one word: Wow! Seventy-two seconds. Then nothing. People have pointed telescopes at that patch of sky again and again. It has never come back. I'm not saying it was aliens. I'm saying nobody has explained it."
 },
